Develop with containers | Docker Docs

1.	To get started, either clone or download the project as a ZIP file to your local machine.
2.	 git clone https://github.com/docker/getting-started-todo-app
And after the project is cloned, navigate into the new directory created by the clone:
 cd getting-started-todo-app
3.	Once you have the project, start the development environment using Docker Compose.
To start the project using the CLI, run the following command:

 docker compose watch

4.	Container is now seen in docker desktop
5.	Docker build -t welcome .

